    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `membershipNumber` following the codebase's existing derived-field pattern (mirroring `getInitials()` in `Person.java`), rather than adding a stored column or duplicating generation logic.\n\n**Two changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a derived `getMembershipNumber()` getter (no column, no setter). It computes the value from the owner's own fields, formatting `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'` where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year, zero-padded via `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`. It returns `null` if either source field is absent.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field. MapStruct then maps it automatically from the entity getter, exactly as it does for `initials` and `customerCode`.\n\nWhy this shape: computing on read guarantees a non-null value at the `GET` response even when clients omit `registrationDate` (the entity's `@PrePersist` defaults it to today), whereas a save-time generator would have to replicate that defaulting. The logic lives in one small single-responsibility getter alongside the fields it derives from, with no new catch-all code.\n\nThe `coreMembershipNumberFormat` acceptance test passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
